  "learnFoundationsNextStepsSectionTitle": "Choose one path to continue",
  "learnFoundationsNextStepsSectionSubtitle": "These next paths stay focused, so you can keep learning without running into a wall of options.",
  "learnFoundationsNextStepsSalahHint": "Choose this if you want to understand prayer, wudu, and the first practical steps of daily worship.",
  "learnFoundationsNextStepsQuranHint": "Choose this if you want a calm way into reading, listening, and reflecting with the Qur’an.",
  "learnFoundationsNextStepsDhikrHint": "Choose this if you want a light daily rhythm of dua and remembrance you can start right away.",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsTitle": "Keep the Habit Going",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsSubtitle": "You have started with meaning and simplicity. Now you can practice gently and connect dhikr to the rest of your worship.",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsIntroTitle": "Use the tool to support the habit, not replace it",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsIntroBody": "The dhikr counter can help you stay present and consistent, but the goal is not numbers alone. Start small, keep your heart engaged, and let remembrance become a quiet daily companion.",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsOpenToolAction": "Open dhikr tool",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsSectionTitle": "What could come next",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsSectionSubtitle": "Choose one nearby path if you want your remembrance to strengthen prayer, character, or your wider daily rhythm.",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsCharacterHint": "Choose this if you want your remembrance to shape patience, adab, and everyday conduct.",
  "learnDailyDhikrNextStepsSalahHint": "Choose this if you want dhikr to stay closely connected to prayer and daily worship.",
  "learnQuranBeginnerSoftBridgeTitle": "Begin with the Qur’an",
  "learnQuranBeginnerSoftBridgeSubtitle": "You do not need to feel fully prepared before you begin. Start small, stay calm, and let understanding grow over time.",
  "learnQuranBeginnerSoftBridgeIntroTitle": "It is okay to begin gently",
  "learnQuranBeginnerSoftBridgeIntroBody": "The Qur’an is guidance and mercy. You do not have to read a lot or understand everything at once. One ayah, one moment of listening, or one small reflection is already a meaningful beginning.",
  "learnQuranBeginnerSoftBridgeHintStartSmall": "Start with one small step. A little steady time with the Qur’an is better than waiting for the perfect moment.",
  "learnQuranBeginnerSoftBridgeHintPace": "You can read, listen, or simply reflect. Move at a pace that feels sincere and sustainable.",
  "learnQuranBeginnerSoftBridgeBeginAction": "Let’s begin",
